<title>UK: DHL to create 500 UK jobs as exports rise.</title>
<headline>DHL to create 500 UK jobs as exports rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Express distribution company DHL Worldwide Express said on Thursday it planned to create 500 new jobs in Britain this year to cope with the demand created by British exporters.</p>
<p>DHL said it currently employed 3,000 workers in Britain. The new jobs would be mainly in sales, customer service and couriers, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The jobs reflect the upward trend in British exports which began in 1996 and looks set to continue during 1997,&quot; DHL said.</p>
<p>It said revenue from British firms rose 24 percent last year and 600 new jobs were created.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
